content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-110 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-24020; applicable manual AQ-OM-300 Revision D.",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing-housing temperature is 92 C and rising. The applicable HF-300 housing-surface limits are normal up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C and trip at 90 C. The reading is therefore 22 C above the normal range, 12 C above alarm and 2 C above trip. Shut down now; the temperature being above the manufacturer's 80 C alarm limit also requires this priority-1 work order to be raised within the shift.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reported vibration is 4.0 mm/s. If this is the bearing-housing velocity RMS measurement required by the manual, Figure 3 places it in Zone B, 2.8–4.5 mm/s RMS, labelled 'Long-term operation'. It is below Zone C at 4.5 and Zone D at 7.1, so this reading alone does not trigger SSP-07's highest-severity-zone immediate-stop and reliability-engineer requirements. The report does not confirm the RMS basis, measurement location or the other housing reading.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing noise has no numeric acoustic limit in the supplied evidence, but Section 5.3 explicitly requires both bearings to be replaced as a pair when either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature. The reported noise and high temperature therefore support paired replacement regardless of the Zone B vibration classification.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear is the leading suspect: it is documented as a cause of both high bearing temperature and high vibration, and the reported bearing noise and high temperature require paired-bearing replacement. Confirm the condition during inspection.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Misalignment is another documented cause common to high bearing temperature and high vibration. Check alignment and correct it to the HF-300 tolerances.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing is a documented cause of high bearing temperature. Check grease quantity; the evidence does not establish whether this pump is over-greased.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage is a documented possible cause of elevated vibration and should be checked during inspection, although the supplied evidence does not confirm it.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Cavitation is a documented possible cause of elevated vibration; check NPSH. No cavitation or NPSH measurements are supplied.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Shut down P-110 immediately and keep it out of service pending inspection and repair because the drive-end housing temperature is 92 C and rising, above the 90 C trip limit. Do not delay shutdown to collect additional vibration readings. Process this as P1 within the shift because the temperature also exceeds the 80 C alarm limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Never run the pump dry during troubleshooting or return-to-service checks. The seal flush is Plan 11 from pump discharge.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before work inside the pump or on its seal, electrically isolate and apply LOTO at the MCC; mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves; drain and vent first and obtain the required line-break permit.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Investigate and record the underlying condition: check grease quantity, inspect the bearings and impeller, check shaft alignment and check NPSH. Use these findings to distinguish bearing wear, over-greasing, misalignment, impeller problems and cavitation rather than assuming a root cause.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before removing the back pull-out assembly for access, obtain a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and use certified lifting equipment. The assembly weighs 68 kg, exceeding the 25 kg lifting-control threshold, and the manual separately requires lifting equipment. The back pull-out design allows removal of the rotating assembly without disturbing the casing or pipework.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Replace both bearings as a pair, not only the drive-end bearing: drive-end bearing HF3-512, 6312-C3, quantity 1; non-drive-end bearing HF3-510, 6310-C3, quantity 1. The reported noise and high temperature meet the Section 5.3 paired-replacement trigger.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Replace casing gasket HF3-120 whenever the casing is opened. For reassembly, use lightly oiled threads and apply the applicable Table 5 torques: bearing-housing bolts M12, 85 Nm; casing bolts M16, 210 Nm if disturbed; impeller nut M24, 160 Nm if removed; seal-gland nuts M10, 25 Nm if seal work is performed.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, perform laser shaft alignment. Limits are 0.05 mm parallel offset and 0.05 mm per 100 mm angular misalignment.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "At return to service after repair, monitor bearing-housing surface temperature against the 70 C normal, 80 C alarm and 90 C trip limits; do not operate at or above the trip limit. Measure vibration velocity on both bearing housings and classify the highest reading using Figure 3, then continue the required weekly monitoring.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If vibration reaches the manufacturer's highest severity zone, Zone D beginning at 7.1 mm/s RMS, stop the pump immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3; replace together with the non-drive-end bearing because either bearing showing noise or high temperature triggers paired replacement.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3; replace as the matching half of the bearing pair.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket, conditional on the casing being opened; the parts list requires replacement whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Immediate shutdown is required by the temperature condition: 92 C exceeds the HF-300 trip limit of 90 C. The vibration reading is not the basis for this shutdown.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Use electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanical isolation of both suction and discharge valves, and a line-break permit with draining and venting completed first for internal pump or seal work.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For the 68 kg back pull-out assembly, use a shift-supervisor-signed lifting plan and certified lifting equipment; this exceeds the 25 kg threshold and lifting equipment is also specifically required by the manual.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Do not run the pump dry; maintain the documented Plan 11 flush arrangement from pump discharge for any operational check.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before line break, confirm whether P-110 is on chemically dosed service. If it is, use chemical goggles and nitrile gloves. The dosing evidence specifically names P-101 through P-106 and does not establish P-110's status.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "A highest-severity-zone vibration result requires an immediate stop and notification of the reliability engineer before restart; the reported 4.0 mm/s value does not itself meet that trigger.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement as a pair: standard labour allowance 6.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment after motor or bearing-housing movement: standard labour allowance 1.5 hours with 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No standard labour times are supplied for isolation, lifting setup, grease checks, bearing and impeller inspection, NPSH investigation or any additional casing or seal work; Table 6 covers only seal replacement, paired-bearing replacement and laser alignment.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "No conflicting asset-specific limit sets are present: AQ-OM-300 Revision D is the HF-300 manual and no alternative serial-range or date-specific limits are supplied for serial HF3-24020. Figure 3's Zone B 'long-term operation' label applies only to vibration and does not override the independent 90 C temperature trip. The temperature limit therefore governs immediate shutdown, while SSP-07 separately governs P1 response and highest-vibration-zone controls.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Was the reported 4.0 mm/s an RMS velocity measured on a bearing housing, which housing was measured, and what is the non-drive-end reading? C06 and C07 require both-housing velocity monitoring and classification of the highest value, but the report does not provide these details.",
    "What grease type and quantity are specified, and what quantity is actually installed? C09 directs a grease-quantity check but supplies no lubrication specification or acceptable quantity.",
    "Is P-110 on a chemically dosed line? C16 identifies only P-101 through P-106, so applicability of the chemical goggles and nitrile gloves required by C15 must be confirmed before work.",
    "What are the final bearing, impeller, alignment and NPSH findings? C09 lists possible causes and checks but does not establish the definitive root cause.",
    "Will the repair scope open the casing or disturb the impeller or mechanical seal? This determines whether the conditional gasket and associated Table 5 fastener requirements in C05 and C11 apply."
  ]
}
